{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine","id":1475571,"title":"Russia's War on Ukraine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-27T22:15:31-08:00","id":1475571,"title":"Russia's War on Ukraine","content":"Just some thoughts I've had and been having about the Ukraine invasion.<br /> <br /> So one thing I've noticed is that there's a lot of head-scratching over why Putin decided to invade all of Ukraine. Many people thought he would stop in Eastern Ukraine but very few thought he would move towards Kyiv. United States intelligence insisting the buildup was for a full invasion was dismissed by many as overblown rhetoric. And then when the invasion did occur, it's turned out to be absolutely inept. The United States made many mistakes in Afghanistan and Iraq, but Russia's invasion of Ukraine has been an absolute shitshow by any metric.<br /> <br /> There were no supply lines. They were sending in tanks that would run out of fuel. Drivers weren't trained on basics like how to get them out of mud. Troops don't know where they're going or what they're doing. Many of them haven't even been given maps. Russia is using tactics that would have already been outdated 50 years ago. Ukraine is claiming to be killing Russians at a rate of 20 for every 1 Ukrainian dying. And that's easy to dismiss as propaganda, but looking at cell phone videos coming out of the conflict, I can honestly believe it considering how absolutely inept the Russian forces are and how massively outdated so much of their equipment is (there was one video where some Ukrainian soldiers are examining a tank that the Russians abandoned and one of them says, &quot;Oh! I know this tank! It's the one my grandfather drove into Germany,&quot; and all of them start laughing at how decrepit so much of the Russian equipment is). So many of the fights seem to involve the Russians stumbling into an ambush, getting picked off like ducks in a row and running away or surrendering. Their convoys are being blown up by drones because Russia hasn't been able to attain air superiority. If it weren't for the fact that so many of the people dying are basically are kids and civilians this would almost seem like a farce.<br /> <br /> I don't want to denigrate Ukrainian bravery and heroics, but at the same time it's kind of staggering to see how bumbling the Russian military has been. I grew up during the Cold War and seeing the myth of Russian military capabilities imploding like this is eye-opening. At the beginning, many people though this was only the first wave - Russia was sending in conscripts with poor equipment to soften things up before sending in their &quot;real&quot; troops with better equipment. But it quickly became apparent that, no, this <i>was</i> the invasion force. There weren't supply lines or preparations for a follow up or anything else.<br /> <br /> I recently came across <a href=\"https://nvo.ng.ru/realty/2022-02-03/3_1175_donbass.html\" target=\"_blank\">an article written by Mikhail Khodarenok back on February 3rd.</a> Note that it's in Russian but Google Translate works pretty well to make it understandable. He was a long-serving member of Russia's High Command and he still regularly communicates with high ranking members of Russia's military. I wish I had seen it earlier because it seems to explain what's going on in Russia and why they invaded Ukraine. This was basically an open letter written as a reaction towards pro-invasion sentiment in High Command trying to point out why the logic that was popular among military elites about how easy an invasion would be was completely wrong and why Russia should throw invasion plans in the trash.<br /> <br /> In short, Russia's high command wildly overestimated their own capability (they believed they would be able to completely disable Ukraine's military in less than an hour, apparently 10 minutes or even fewer were were commonly being thrown around). They also completely underestimated Ukraine's military, not seeming to have realized that Ukraine had been in the process of completely updating its military tactics and equipment since 2014. Finally High Command seems to have fallen for its own propaganda and believed that most Ukrainians truly loathed Zelenskyy, absolutely loved Russia, and would welcome a Russian invasion with open arms and immediately put down their arms. Which is baffling to me. The attitude seems to have been that an invasion of Ukraine would be over in less than a day, that Russia wouldn't even really need to send in forces, that the Ukrainians themselves would overthrow the government and willingly join Russia, and that by the time the world even began considering sanctions, the war would be over and Ukraine would have joined Russia. It's reminiscent of the US attitude towards Iraq, that we would be welcomed as &quot;liberators&quot; and everything would be rosy, but turned up to 11.<br /> <br /> Here is the article run through Google Translate (also damn Google Translate has gotten really good):<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Some representatives of the Russian political class today argue that Russia is able to inflict a crushing defeat on Ukraine in a few hours (and shorter periods are also mentioned) if a military conflict breaks out. Let's see how such statements correspond to reality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the expert community of Russia, the opinion has recently taken root quite strongly that it will not even be necessary to send troops to the territory of Ukraine, since the Armed Forces of this country are in a deplorable state.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Some political analysts emphasize that a powerful Russian fire strike will destroy almost all surveillance and communication systems, artillery and tank formations. Moreover, a number of experts conclude that even one crushing blow from Russia will be enough to end such a war.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As a cherry on the cake, some analysts emphasize the fact that no one in Ukraine will defend the \u201cKyiv regime\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>NO EASY WALK</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Let's start with the last one. To assert that no one in Ukraine will defend the regime means, in practice, complete ignorance of the military-political situation and the mood of the broad masses of the people in the neighboring state. Moreover, the degree of hatred (which, as you know, is the most effective fuel for armed struggle) in the neighboring republic in relation to Moscow is frankly underestimated. No one will meet the Russian army with bread, salt and flowers in Ukraine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It seems that the events in the south-east of Ukraine in 2014 did not teach anyone anything. Then, after all, they also expected that the entire left-bank Ukraine, in a single impulse and in a matter of seconds, would turn into Novorossia. We have already drawn maps, estimated the personnel of future administrations of cities and regions, and developed state flags.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">But even the Russian-speaking population of this part of Ukraine (including such cities as Kharkov, Zaporozhye, Dnepropetrovsk, Mariupol) did not support such plans in their vast majority. The project &quot;Novorossiya&quot; was somehow imperceptibly blown away and quietly died.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In a word, the liberation campaign in 2022, following the model and likeness of 1939, will not work out in any way. In this case, the words of the classic of Soviet literature Arkady Gaidar are more true than ever: \u201cIt is clear that we will now have not an easy battle, but a hard battle.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>&quot;BY A SMALL BLOOD, A POWERFUL BLOW&quot;</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now about the &quot;powerful fire strike by Russia&quot;, which allegedly will destroy &quot;practically all surveillance and communication systems, artillery and tank formations of the Armed Forces of Ukraine.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This expression alone shows that only political workers could say such a thing. For reference: in the course of hypothetical military operations on the scale of a theater of operations, strikes are carried out on priority targets and massive fire strikes. Note that in the course of operational-strategic planning, the epithets \u201cpowerful\u201d (as well as \u201cmedium\u201d, \u201cweak\u201d, etc.) are not used.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Military science emphasizes that strikes can be strategic (this mostly applies to strategic nuclear forces), operational and tactical. According to the number of forces involved and objects hit, strikes can be massive, group and single. It is still better not to introduce or use other concepts, even in works of a political science nature.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Attacks on priority targets and massive fire strikes can be carried out within the framework of the front (fronts on the western borders of Russia have not yet been formed) or the main command of the armed forces in the theater of operations (so far, one has not been created in the South-Western strategic direction either). Anything less than that is no longer a massive hit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And what is, for example, a massive fire strike (MOA) of the front? To begin with, we note that the maximum number of combat-ready forces and means of aviation, missile troops and artillery, electronic warfare equipment at the disposal of the commander of the front forces (operational-strategic formation) is involved in the MOU. The MOU consists of one massive air sortie, two or three launches of OTP and TR missile systems, and several artillery fire raids. Well, if the degree of fire damage to the enemy is 60-70%.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">What is the most important thing in this matter in relation to the conflict with Ukraine? Of course, the MOU will inflict heavy losses on a potential enemy. But to expect to crush the armed forces of an entire state with just one such blow means to show simply unbridled optimism in the course of planning and conducting combat operations. In the course of hypothetical strategic actions on the theater of operations, such MOUs will have to be applied not one or two, but much more.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It must be added by all means that the reserves of promising and high-precision weapons in the RF Armed Forces are not of any unlimited nature. Hypersonic missiles of the Zircon type are not yet in service. And the number of Kalibr (sea-launched cruise missiles), Kinzhals, Kh-101 (air-launched cruise missiles) and Iskander missiles is measured in the hundreds at best (tens in the case of Kinzhals). This arsenal is absolutely not enough to wipe out a state the size of France and with a population of more than 40 million from the face of the Earth. Namely, Ukraine is characterized by such parameters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>ABOUT AIR SUPERIORITY</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Sometimes it is asserted in the Russian expert community (by fans of the Douai doctrine) that since the hypothetical military operations in Ukraine will take place under the conditions of complete dominance of Russian aircraft in the air, the war will be extremely short and will end in the shortest possible time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">At the same time, it is somehow forgotten that the armed formations of the Afghan opposition during the conflict of 1979-1989 did not have a single aircraft and not a single combat helicopter. And the war in this country dragged on for as much as 10 years. The Chechen fighters did not have a single aircraft either. And the fight against them lasted for several years and cost the federal forces a lot of blood and casualties.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And the Armed Forces of Ukraine still have some kind of combat aircraft. As well as means of air defense.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">By the way, the Ukrainian crews of the anti-aircraft missile forces (by no means Georgian ones) significantly pinched the Russian Air Force during the 2008 conflict. After the first day of hostilities, the leadership of the Russian Air Force was in frank shock from the losses incurred. And you shouldn't forget about it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>MOURNED IN ADVANCE</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now about the thesis &quot;The Armed Forces of Ukraine are in a deplorable state.&quot; Of course, the Armed Forces of Ukraine have problems with aviation and modern air defense systems. But the following must also be acknowledged. If until 2014 the Armed Forces of Ukraine were a fragment of the Soviet army, over the past seven years a qualitatively different army has been created in Ukraine, on a completely different ideological basis and largely on NATO standards. And very modern weapons and equipment are being supplied and continue to be supplied to Ukraine from many countries of the North Atlantic Alliance.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As for the weakest point of the Armed Forces of Ukraine - the Air Force. It cannot be ruled out that the collective West may, in a fairly short time, supply Kiev with fighters, as they say, from the presence of the armed forces - in other words, second-hand. However, this second-hand, in terms of its tactical and technical characteristics, will be quite comparable with the majority of aircraft in the Russian fleet.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Of course, today the Armed Forces of Ukraine are significantly inferior to the Armed Forces of the Russian Federation in terms of their combat and operational capabilities. No one doubts this, neither in the East nor in the West.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">But this army cannot be taken lightly either. In this regard, one must always remember the testament of Alexander Suvorov: &quot;Never despise your enemy, do not consider him stupider and weaker than you.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now with regard to the assertion that Western countries will not send a single soldier to die for Ukraine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It should be noted that this is likely to be the case. However, in the event of Russia's invasion, this does not at all rule out massive assistance to the Armed Forces of Ukraine from the collective West with a wide variety of weapons and military equipment and bulk deliveries of all kinds of materiel. In this regard, the West has already shown a consolidated position, unprecedented until now, which, it seems, was not predicted in Moscow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">There is no doubt that the United States and the countries of the North Atlantic Alliance will begin a kind of reincarnation of Lend-Lease, modeled after the Second World War, there is no doubt. An influx of volunteers from the West, which can be very numerous, is not ruled out.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>PARTISANS AND UNDERGROUND</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And finally, about the duration of a hypothetical campaign. In the Russian expert community, several hours are called, sometimes even several tens of minutes. At the same time, it is somehow forgotten that we have already gone through all this. The phrase &quot;take the city with one airborne regiment in two hours&quot; has already become a classic of the genre.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It is also worth recalling that the mighty Stalinist NKVD and the multi-million Soviet army fought the nationalist underground in Western Ukraine for more than 10 years. And now there is an option that the whole of Ukraine can easily go into the partisans. In addition, these formations can easily begin to operate already on the territory of Russia.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The armed struggle in large Ukrainian cities is generally difficult to predict. It is common knowledge that the big city is the best battlefield for the weak and less technically advanced side of the armed conflict.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Serious experts emphasize that in a metropolis it is possible not only to concentrate a grouping of thousands and even tens of thousands of fighters, but also to hide it from the superior firepower of the enemy. And also to supply it with material resources for a long time and make up for losses in people and equipment. Neither mountains, nor forests, nor jungles today provide such an opportunity.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Experts are convinced that the urban environment helps the defenders, slows down the movement of the attackers, allows you to place a record number of fighters per unit area, and compensates for the lag in forces and technologies. And in Ukraine there are more than enough large cities, including those with a million inhabitants. So the Russian army in the course of a hypothetical war with Ukraine may meet with far more than just Stalingrad and Grozny.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b>CONCLUSIONS</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In general, there will be no Ukrainian blitzkrieg. The statements of some experts such as \u201cThe Russian army will defeat most of the units of the Armed Forces of Ukraine in 30-40 minutes\u201d, \u201cRussia is able to defeat Ukraine in 10 minutes in the event of a full-scale war\u201d, \u201cRussia will defeat Ukraine in eight minutes\u201d have no serious grounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">And finally, the most important thing. An armed conflict with Ukraine is currently fundamentally not in Russia's national interests. Therefore, it is best for some overexcited Russian experts to forget about their hatred fantasies. And in order to prevent further reputational losses, never remember again.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So the situation now is that Russia is stuck in a quagmire. They thought the war would be over immediately and that Ukraine would willingly join Russia. Now they're realizing that they are going to have be stuck fighting for years or decades. Russia doesn't want to be fighting that long and can't be able to afford it in the face of the massive sanctions they're facing. Their economy will collapse long before Ukraine's will to fight does. So that's where Russia is right now, and I think Khodarenok's response gives some good ideas for how Russia got here and why the invasion into Ukraine has seemed like something the Three Stooges put together.<br /> <br /> To note, in the Russian media they have been very careful to continually frame this as a &quot;special operation&quot; for the purpose of &quot;de-Nazifying&quot; Ukraine rather than a war. This basically means that Russia can declare that they have succeeded in de-Nazifying Ukraine and pull back whenever they want. One possibility is that Putin just wants Zelenskyy dead. Once he's dead Putin will say, &quot;Mission Accomplished, we de-Nazified Ukraine&quot; and will then pull Russian troops back to Eastern Ukraine and demand that the sanctions on Russia stop. But Zelenskyy is providing much harder to kill than Putin imagined. Russia's planners likely thought he would flee the country the moment they invaded and the government would swiftly collapse. I don't think they ever planned on him being willing to fight to death.<br /> <br /> But, it's likely that Putin's biggest worry right now is that if he does pull Russian troops out of Ukraine proper and back to the eastern territory, Ukraine will respond by conceding the territory that Russia took in Crimea and the East and then immediately ask for membership in NATO and have that granted. Just a few weeks ago it was impossible to imagine Ukraine would willingly give up its territory, but it was also impossible to imagine Russia attacking Kyiv and it's always difficult to tell what Putin is thinking. So it's possible he may decide to keep troops in Ukraine indefinitely, even though that would bleed Russia dry both in terms of money and manpower, because that would be only way he could ensure that Ukraine could not join NATO (regardless of whether Ukraine actually would do so or not).<br /> <br /> Of course now US intelligence is suggesting Belarus might be joining the war on Russia's side and there's no telling what will happen, if Russia and Belarus will be able to disentangle themselves from Ukraine, and whether or not other countries will get involved if Belarus does join in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-28-2022, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T23:43:17-08:00","id":1475572,"title":"","content":"Well damn... It looks like politicos everywhere in the world are as utterly self-deluded as they are here in the U.S. I'm not sure if that's comforting or nauseating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T22:49:36-08:00","id":1475714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475572#post1475572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well damn... It looks like politicos everywhere in the world are as utterly self-deluded as they are here in the U.S. I'm not sure if that's comforting or nauseating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are, and this is nauseating, because they're playing with resources and decisions that affect too many lives. People die on their idiocy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T15:12:13-08:00","id":1475744,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, Using a degraded military to invade Ukraine is trading trash for treasure. One thing that should not be ignored is the presence in Russia of an antiwar movement risking being disappeared by the Putin Regime to communicate to the world their opposition to this invasion. The longer he tries to hold Ukraine, the more cause this movement will have to organize against the tyrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475572#post1475572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well damn... It looks like politicos everywhere in the world are as utterly self-deluded as they are here in the U.S. I'm not sure if that's comforting or nauseating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pentagon and its corporate partners intend for there to be at least one war in some part of the world at all times, for the next hundred years, in order to sustain their massive budget. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475714#post1475714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they are, and this is nauseating, because they're playing with resources and decisions that affect too many lives. People die on their idiocy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but agree with a lot of commentators who point out that Joe Biden's observable cognitive decline invites Russia and China to move forward with covetous military agendas. I don't fault <i>him</i> for it, but the DNC for propping him up. He should be in a care facility and there should be an alternative to Trump who is sharp enough to handle the geopolitical situation in a way that does not result in a nuclear atrocity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zB0W91E3XOU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zB0W91E3XOU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zB0W91E3XOU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zB0W91E3XOU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T16:49:52-08:00","id":1475753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475744#post1475744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but agree with a lot of commentators who point out that Joe Biden's observable cognitive decline invites Russia and China to move forward with covetous military agendas. I don't fault <i>him</i> for it, but the DNC for propping him up. He should be in a care facility and there should be an alternative to Trump who is sharp enough to handle the geopolitical situation in a way that does not result in a nuclear atrocity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can put the blame for Russia's invasion on anyone other than Putin. Russia would have invaded Ukraine no matter who was President of the US. This was something that Putin has wanted to do for a very long time, he's personally written papers about how Ukraine's identity is that of Russia and needs to be brought back into Russia, and ultimately it wouldn't have mattered if Biden or Bernie or Trump or anyone else was President of the US, Russia would still be bombing Kyiv right now.<br /> <br /> Pointing at Biden is giving the US far too much credit and Putin not enough credit. Ultimately Putin was convinced after multiple US presidential administrations failed to appropriately respond or handle Afghanistan, Iraq, Syria, and Russia's earlier invasions of Georgia, Crimea and Donbass that the current administration would not act any differently from Bush's, Obama's or Trump's. That was a gamble that he lost because not only did the current administration act decisively, the whole world has as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-03-2022, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T17:21:58-08:00","id":1475755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475753#post1475753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you can put the blame for Russia's invasion on anyone other than Putin. Russia would have invaded Ukraine no matter who was President of the US. This was something that Putin has wanted to do for a very long time, he's personally written papers about how Ukraine's identity is that of Russia and needs to be brought back into Russia, and ultimately it wouldn't have mattered if Biden or Bernie or Trump or anyone else was President of the US, Russia would still be bombing Kyiv right now.<br /> <br /> Pointing at Biden is giving the US too much credit and Putin not enough credit. Ultimately Putin was convinced after multiple US presidential administrations failed to appropriately respond or handle Afghanistan, Iraq, Syria, and Russia's earlier invasions of Georgia, Crimea and Donbass that the current administration would not act any differently from Bush's, Obama's or Trump's. That was a gamble that he lost because not only did the current administration act decisively, the whole world has as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In any decision, there are major and minor factors. The existing major factors like the gains Putin expected to come from invasion he thought would be a cakewalk could be enough to determine the decision, regardless of minor factors, but if you control the minor factor of what leader the American superpower presents to the world, it's worth choosing one that would do the most to deter expansionism by dictators.<br /> <br /> I can't see an attempted long term annexation of Ukraine succeeding, given the punishing resistance of the Ukrainians. My hope is that the antiwar movement in Russia will succeed in ousting him. It may end up that they draw logistical support from victorious defenders in Ukraine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T20:32:15-08:00","id":1475762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475755#post1475755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any decision, there are major and minor factors. The existing major factors like the gains Putin expected to come from invasion he thought would be a cakewalk could be enough to determine the decision, regardless of minor factors, but if you control the minor factor of what leader the American superpower presents to the world, it's worth choosing one that would do the most to deter expansionism by dictators.<br /> <br /> I can't see an attempted long term annexation of Ukraine succeeding, given the punishing resistance of the Ukrainians. My hope is that the antiwar movement in Russia will succeed in ousting him. It may end up that they draw logistical support from victorious defenders in Ukraine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing is that Putin was under the impression that the invasion would take a day or less. That by the time the US and other countries realized what was happening and and got together to decide on a united response, the war would already be over and Ukraine would be part of Russia. Basically he gambled that it would be a fait accompli. That's why the US response or who was President was essentially a non-issue since any US response would already be &quot;after the fact&quot; of Ukraine's loss and Russia's victory.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Putin vastly overestimated Russia's capabilities while vastly underestimating Ukraine's ability to respond and also buying into his own propaganda that Ukrainians hated the &quot;Kyiv regime&quot; would either throw down their weapons to join Russia or would overthrow the government of Ukraine. What he thought was going to be an invasion that would be over in a few hours has turned into a war that's lasted a week, and will likely last for many more. Even if Russia is able to take Kyiv, they're going to be stuck fighting a war in Ukraine for decades, and then consider that even the most conservative estimates suggest that Russia has already had more soldiers die in one week in Ukraine than the United States lost in almost 20 years in Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> Ultimately if there is any cognitive decline or decline in decision making going on, it would seem to be coming from Putin, who apparently has lost his composure and ability to think clearly. Long time people who have been watching Putin or have a history of interacting with Putin all seem to agree that Putin's actions and statements in the past few weeks have been extremely out of character.<br /> <br /> Putin's statements about righting historical wrongs, and the grand and undeniable destiny of Russia, and the the insidious conspiracies of the West, more resemble things you'd expect to hear from Kim Jong-un than the sort of stuff that Putin would have been saying just a few years ago. Even something like the way he just utterly humiliated his Director of Foreign Intelligence, Sergey Naryshkin on TV was very out of character. Putin's always been harsh on people who worked for him, but never to the point of blatantly and publicly demeaning them like that. He almost always dresses people down in private, never in public and definitely not on national TV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T21:13:50-08:00","id":1475763,"title":"","content":"I found a lengthy recent video with four experts analyzing Putin's body language. It's all about the invasion: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCXGQzuaNic\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCXGQzuaNic</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T22:05:56-08:00","id":1475879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475755#post1475755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what leader the American superpower presents to the world, it's worth choosing one that would do the most to deter expansionism by dictators.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a bad thing to do right now. Very bad thing to do.<br /> <br /> First, we have to avoid giving a president more credit than their due. Those analysis and decisions are complex and involve a lot of people. I don't see, given the general context, another US president making a difference. What was there to do? Sending military help would just escalate things even more and justify the Russian invasion. The discourse was already as harsh as it could be. The EU took a larger role this time, which was good. The US being more proactive here would just make things look more like unilateral influence and escalate the conflict, causing even more turmoil and death.<br /> <br /> Second, there are many reasons to play down the whole &quot;American superpower deterring dictators&quot; thing. This has been a sore point for a lot of people for a long time, and in last decades the world politics has changed a lot on how much it accepts US's self-portrayal as defenders of the globe. Trump did a wonderful job on burying the last notion that the world should still see the US as fair on its relations and a sensible neutral party.<br /> <br /> It is not to say that the US shouldn't take a stance, as everyone should, and it is actually doing so in the matter. But doing so in this way would only increase suspicion on its participation for no reason.<br /> <br /> Currently, the US rivals as world powers, Russia and China, capitalize a lot on pointing out how much the US intervenes abroad as the &quot;world leader&quot;, mixing propaganda to style itself as a liberator with militarily or economically bullying others into accepting its unilateral decisions. It is important for its diplomacy, international influence and, on the case at hand, peacekeeping, that the US take a less direct and personal approach and work more as an equal to other countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T11:19:22-08:00","id":1475919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually a bad thing to do right now. Very bad thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean choosing a Presidential Candidate who tries to suborn foreign heads of state with threats and swagger. I mean choosing one that is not so old that they are likely to face cognitive decline while in office. The choosing was done by the DNC before the last election and there were already signs of Biden having difficulties then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, we have to avoid giving a president more credit than their due. Those analysis and decisions are complex and involve a lot of people. I don't see, given the general context, another US president making a difference. What was there to do? Sending military help would just escalate things even more and justify the Russian invasion. The discourse was already as harsh as it could be. The EU took a larger role this time, which was good. The US being more proactive here would just make things look more like unilateral influence and escalate the conflict, causing even more turmoil and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putin met Biden met in Geneva on June 21st, 2021. It would have been obvious to Putin that the President has serious cognitive difficulties. Another President would have demonstrated that the American government had its highest office occupied by someone who does not have to be handled by staff. When the President has to be handled by staffers of obviously lower authority, it destabilizes the government. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, there are many reasons to play down the whole &quot;American superpower deterring dictators&quot; thing. This has been a sore point for a lot of people for a long time, and in last decades the world politics has changed a lot on how much it accepts US's self-portrayal as defenders of the globe.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a lot that I could say in agreement about this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Trump did a wonderful job on burying the last notion that the world should still see the US as fair on its relations and a sensible neutral party.</div> </div> </div> </div>A guy who has a life sized portrait of himself made with money intended for charity definitely has psychological issues which should also disqualify him from being President. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not to say that the US shouldn't take a stance, as everyone should, and it is actually doing so in the matter. But doing so in this way would only increase suspicion on its participation for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I have to state that I meant &quot;Put forward someone who is all there.&quot;, not &quot;Send a tough guy.&quot;. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475879#post1475879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, the US rivals as world powers, Russia and China, capitalize a lot on pointing out how much the US intervenes abroad as the &quot;world leader&quot;, mixing propaganda to style itself as a liberator with militarily or economically bullying others into accepting its unilateral decisions. It is important for its diplomacy, international influence and, on the case at hand, peacekeeping, that the US take a less direct and personal approach and work more as an equal to other countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much is the world swayed by China's PRC Government? I have seen what I could stand to watch of an outdoor organ market where a government official was auctioning a person.. I mean, it is difficult to describe. China can hire the most eloquence speakers in the world and it will still be difficult to believe anything they say. As for Russia's criticism of the U.S., perhaps before Putin invaded Ukraine, this had some weight to it. <br /> <br /> A community of nations working together to apply economic pressure through sanctions (the Ruble is now worth less than the in-game currency of Clash of Clans) in order to restore peace is desirable. The same expectations for cognitive functionality should apply to each head of state. Anyone who is going to represent their country within that community should know what is going on around them. The only member that I know of who is in serious question as to his wherewithal is Joe Biden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T17:39:22-08:00","id":1475954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1475919#post1475919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putin met Biden met in Geneva on June 21st, 2021. It would have been obvious to Putin that the President has serious cognitive difficulties. Another President would have demonstrated that the American government had its highest office occupied by someone who does not have to be handled by staff. When the President has to be handled by staffers of obviously lower authority, it destabilizes the government.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is spreading political disinformation and to do so again will result in being banned. Take an infraction.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T19:51:11-08:00","id":1475961,"title":"","content":"Regarding the situation directly between Russia and Ukraine, my heart is with the antiwar movement protesting across Russia and the Ukrainians fighting to repel the invasion of their country.. Down with Vladimir Putin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-07-2022, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T00:02:29-08:00","id":1475969,"title":"","content":"Biden isn't the only head of state facing suspicion of cognitive limitations, mental health issues and/or emotional instability. This is actually a fairly common things all across the world, in many forms and intensities. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> said, Putin himself is facing such suspicions lately and that may very well be true. The same way that for Biden it may very well not be, unless we have some official diagnosis. Mental health is far more complex than the ease we have at pointing perceived lack and explaining it as such.<br /> <br /> Presidents have to deal with a lot of things they don't actually understand well enough. While they are powerful people indeed, the notion that they lead the nation by themselves is mostly for show in any sane government. Putin has actual absolute power because he <b>is</b> a dictator, but Biden and any other American president is not, it is fully expected that he has staff handling a lot of things for him. <b>Putin</b>, as many dictators, put a lot of effort into selling an image of personal prowess and self-sufficiency, but that's not how things actually work anywhere.<br /> <br /> China and Russia don't need to convince you that they're reasonable. They capitalize in the fact that the US isn't either, and any opportunity to argue that foreign sanctions are just the US being unreasonable. International politics is not a common debate, who they're trying to sway is their own people first and some key international players second, and those players are also politicians that will take the argument not as a thing to convince them, but as a tool for them to put forward their own interests and discourse. It is not how much they appear in the right, it is how much they can play the victim when the US points a finger.<br /> <br /> If you think that Biden is the only member of the international community facing serious question as to his wherewithal, then you need to look more into the details of politics of other countries and the charges they face from their opponents in their own countries. From the top of my head I remember some very intense debates of this nature about Bolsonaro, Putin, Macron, Johnson and Xi Jinping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T01:35:40-08:00","id":1475975,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat limited in the way I can reply and not even sure where those limits lie. Myself, I have a condition that affects concentration. It is not something I readily admit to, because it affects how much I can read and that advantages someone trying to prove you wrong at times. I detest Canadian Winter and have my brain locked on the date, March 21st, the beginning of Spring. So, I substituted a date I was copying with 21.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind the question about extrapolation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-07-2022, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T18:50:30-08:00","id":1476017,"title":"","content":"One thing I find interesting. Back during the 80's, when Ronald Reagan was president, he was being hit by early Alzheimer's while in officer. There were people who worked with him or interviewed him who noticed his mental decline. You could even sometimes get glimpses of this on TV where he would be saying something, ramble for a bit, forget what he was saying and then his wife Nancy or an aide would whisper to him to get him back on track. <br /> <br /> The news media didn't play that up, didn't discuss it and did their best not to draw attention to it. There were legitimate worries about how that would affect US relations with other countries, especially the USSR, if they thought the US president wasn't all there mentally. Even more liberal reporters who didn't like Reagan recognized the dangers of drawing attention to his mental state. The USSR, and other foreign powers, would do what it could to take advantage of real, or imagined weakness in US presidents. And that was true even earlier. Going back decades, for the most part, the press might attack a president on policy, but in terms of personal capability the press would never try and present the president as weak because of the worries about how that might end up helping the USA's enemies.<br /> <br /> Compare that to today where certain partisan media groups can't stop telling everyone that Joe Biden is mentally incapable. Whether that's true or not, for people in governments such as Russia's or Chinese, they hear these things and believe them. In those countries the press would never say something like that about a sitting leader, and the fact that you are hearing such things in the US is &quot;proof&quot; that Joe Biden is not capable of running the country (nevermind that the press saying such a thing is the result of the First Amendment which those countries don't have so Biden's inability to crack down on people speaking poorly of him doesn't mean he's mentally incapable).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T20:27:08-08:00","id":1476021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476017#post1476017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compare that to today where certain partisan media groups can't stop telling everyone that Joe Biden is mentally incapable. Whether that's true or not, for people in governments such as Russia's or Chinese, they hear these things and believe them. In those countries the press would never say something like that about a sitting leader, and the fact that you are hearing such things in the US is &quot;proof&quot; that Joe Biden is not capable of running the country (nevermind that the press saying such a thing is the result of the First Amendment which those countries don't have so Biden's inability to crack down on people speaking poorly of him doesn't mean he's mentally incapable).</div> </div> </div> </div>So much so that similar phenomena is observe in every place where the fundamental democratic rights still hold to a sensible degree. Brazil, France, UK, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> What makes the last presidents the most appointed as personally inept isn't a fall on &quot;presidential quality&quot;, but a change in society and politics around the world. Institutions matter more than individuals, information spread too quickly, we're living in a fundamentally distinct society from the one of the old Cold War, even if we end up in a new Cold War. The logic of painting the president as a superman doesn't hold water anymore and actually backfires more than not.<br /> <br /> But on the matter of Ukraine, I've seen some recent news about worrying movements of troops too close to nuclear facilities. I really, really wish that the Russian Army does not get dumber than moving through Chernobyl. Although I must say that I really feel sorry for the actual soldiers in there, as their lives mean nothing to their superiors even by other armies' standards (and they're very low).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T21:12:56-08:00","id":1476025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476021#post1476021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes the last presidents the most appointed as personally inept isn't a fall on &quot;presidential quality&quot;, but a change in society and politics around the world. Institutions matter more than individuals, information spread too quickly, we're living in a fundamentally distinct society from the one of the old Cold War, even if we end up in a new Cold War. The logic of painting the president as a superman doesn't hold water anymore and actually backfires more than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about &quot;superman&quot; but there was the idea that it was in the country's best interest to paint the president as at least reasonably competent rather than continually painting the president as completely and totally incompetent. That that would hurt the country's standing on the world stage and possibly cause other major issues as well. As you say, there are many reasons for this change, it's just something I've noticed and found interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T21:18:26-08:00","id":1476026,"title":"","content":"About 1/4 of Ukraine's electricity comes from nuclear reactors at only four locations. Seizing them, along with cutting Ukraine off from Russian fossil fuels, would cripple Ukraine's modern military forces faster than Russia's current war operations have otherwise proven capable of. It also seems like Russia has given up on annexing Ukraine directly, and has started devastating Ukrainian infrastructure, most of which Ukraine will need Russia's help to rebuild unless the rest of Europe/NATO are willing to go full Marshall Plan after this is over; implying Putin wants to own Ukraine by holding all the infrastructure resources he can to force them to comply to his demands. We can only hope that's the only reason they're doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T01:09:56-08:00","id":1476031,"title":"","content":"An ex-CIA YouTuber I subscribe to made a post about the increase in costs of supplies humanitarian agencies are trying to get to Ukrainians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YnEl4eRhUe8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YnEl4eRhUe8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YnEl4eRhUe8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YnEl4eRhUe8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T06:04:44-08:00","id":1476042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476026#post1476026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About 1/4 of Ukraine's electricity comes from nuclear reactors at only four locations. Seizing them, along with cutting Ukraine off from Russian fossil fuels, would cripple Ukraine's modern military forces faster than Russia's current war operations have otherwise proven capable of. It also seems like Russia has given up on annexing Ukraine directly, and has started devastating Ukrainian infrastructure, most of which Ukraine will need Russia's help to rebuild unless the rest of Europe/NATO are willing to go full Marshall Plan after this is over; implying Putin wants to own Ukraine by holding all the infrastructure resources he can to force them to comply to his demands. We can only hope that's the only reason they're doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the nuclear plants is that they're really sensible to intervention. They <b>are</b> safe, but as someone said (I don't remember where), not <i><b>passively</b></i> safe. They need continuous maintenance and resources, with a minimum of hiccups in the way, like always preferring to have staff with experience with that particular plant instead of trying to change everyone overnight. <br /> <br /> So while Russia may want to somehow control the plants, affecting their actual workings is a bad idea. Even affecting their supplies indirectly is a bad idea. Curiously on of their risks is to be cut off from electricity for example, or have problems with water supply that is used in reactor coolers. Those are the kinds of things that can't happen, or there will be a disaster.<br /> <br /> Russia know this, or at least the Russian nuclear authorities know this. And the action seems to not be geared towards targeting the plants on purpose, at least for now. But the fear is that the Russian military will either take the risks or ignore warnings and do something stupid. Not something stupid like targeting the plants on purpose, but something stupid like damaging vital infrastructure for their operations on accident, as many of the weapons being seen near the plants aren't that reliable on damage control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T12:50:35-08:00","id":1476060,"title":"","content":"I think what you're referring to is what happens if the reactors get shut down (which normally drastically reduces risks during disasters and so on). Normally, nuclear reactors power their own cooling systems, but if you shut one down, they still need cooling. So you need something else powering the process to cool them.<br /> <br /> What I've read from experts that have discussed it, is that they're worried about Russian attacks on the rest of the Ukraine's infrastructure combined with their refusal to honor humanitarian and disaster corridors to allow non-fighters to deal with these things in the middle of a war zone. Basically, modern reactors are designed to endure acute disasters and incidents, that only last a day or two before emergency crews can restore certain safety features. They're not designed for a siege where their emergency diesel generators for their cooling systems can't get refueled on a regular basis after the reactor is shut down and the plant can't access the main grid for that power.<br /> <br /> The concern around staff is that understandably Ukrainians don't want to go to work in a war zone. In the places Russia has taken over the nuclear facilities already, they're reported to be forcing the Ukrainian staff to continue to work instead of trying to replace them with Russians (which probably isn't too hard to do in the short term considering the consequences, but I'm sure those Ukrainians are worried that it's just a matter of time before the Russians are familiar enough with the reactors to run them themselves). So that's even more worries that the staff in other facilities are going to flee rather than stay and operate the reactors as safely as possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T01:16:07-08:00","id":1476196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476060#post1476060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what you're referring to is what happens if the reactors get shut down (which normally drastically reduces risks during disasters and so on). Normally, nuclear reactors power their own cooling systems, but if you shut one down, they still need cooling. So you need something else powering the process to cool them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more like the control systems need to be powered by outside source as a security reason, so if something goes wrong they won't fail first. Although they probably are hooked up to more than on power source (because, while Ukrainians seem to be concerned about Chernobyl getting cut off from outside electricity and are working hard on restoring pwoer to there, they don't seem to be panicking at the moment so it's probably not at the critical stage yet).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T20:24:19-07:00","id":1476355,"title":"","content":"Air-striking a maternity hospital is beyond psychopathic. To prevent nuclear war, the international community will have to avoid creating a situation where Russia feels there is an existential threat to it and they will have to acknowledge Putin as head of state in negotiations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T22:31:37-07:00","id":1476361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476355#post1476355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air-striking a maternity hospital is beyond psychopathic. To prevent nuclear war, the international community will have to avoid creating a situation where Russia feels there is an existential threat to it and they will have to acknowledge Putin as head of state in negotiations.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree, unfortunately it is also common practice across wars. The US bombed several healthcare facilities in Afghanistan and Iraq, and Israel does this in Palestine with alarming frequency (lets hope it diminishes now that Netanyahu is out of the picture, that man is a monster). This is indefensible, but between hypocrisy and politics the narrative will be heavily used by all sides for their own political agenda, not for the actual well being of the survivors.<br /> <br /> On the acknowledgement of Putin, I don't actually see it not being the case at all, do you care to elaborate? As far as I see, Putin was never <b>not</b> recognized as a head of state, and one of the most powerful and dangerous ones at that, he is well taken seriously, contrary to Kim Jong-Un.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T23:52:49-07:00","id":1476365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476361#post1476361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(lets hope it diminishes now that Netanyahu is out of the picture, that man is a monster).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to derail... but Naftali Bennett is worse. The only positive is that he openly agreed to not enact his worse-than-Bebe policies regarding the Palestinian people in order to get support of enough of the Israeli left to get rid of Netanyahu. If Bennett gets enough support from the Israeli right next elections with Netanyahu out of the way, he'll do way worse than Netanyahu did to the Palestinians.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T08:40:50-07:00","id":1476382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476361#post1476361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree, unfortunately it is also common practice across wars. The US bombed several healthcare facilities in Afghanistan and Iraq, and Israel does this in Palestine with alarming frequency (lets hope it diminishes now that Netanyahu is out of the picture, that man is a monster). This is indefensible, but between hypocrisy and politics the narrative will be heavily used by all sides for their own political agenda, not for the actual well being of the survivors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I regarded George Bush Junior, Donald Rumsfeld, Dickhead Cheney and the rest of that Administration as a group of psychopaths - religious fundamentalist psychopaths, to be more specific. I was for the idea of bringing them before the International Criminal Court for war crimes. Joe Biden, to be fair to him, can do little harm compared to them on his worst day. Few people equate criticism of American Presidents with being against Americans. I like what Israel is doing with Sand and Sea, but because I oppose this one policy they have toward the Palestinians, I have to make endless clarifications when the subject comes up. My girlfriend is Jewish, though not religiously so. I love her dearly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476361#post1476361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the acknowledgement of Putin, I don't actually see it not being the case at all, do you care to elaborate? As far as I see, Putin was never <b>not</b> recognized as a head of state, and one of the most powerful and dangerous ones at that, he is well taken seriously, contrary to Kim Jong-Un.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comment was narrowly focused on Putin. Years ago, famous figures in the Russian opposition tried to convince the world not to treat him as a legitimate head of state, citing election fuckery and internal repression. What I am saying is that they will have to continue to meet with him and allow him this status <i>after</i> his forces attacked a maternity hospital - because newborn babies and expectant mothers are such a threat to Russian forces. There is no justification for that and the fact that other heads of state may have normalized this kind of thing doesn't change how I see a person who is responsible for his forces' actions.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, following your comment about taking interest in foreign heads of state, which I used to do a lot more, I saw some reporting on Ji Jinping 's enemies. Serious intrigue happening in the PRC. I tend to be more curious about what powerful multinational corporations are doing than who was most recently elected in Europe, since the former usually controls the later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-14-2022, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T01:04:01-07:00","id":1476420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476382#post1476382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few people equate criticism of American Presidents with being against Americans.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is the opposite. On one hand, a number of Americans get defensive if a foreigner criticize their presidents and take it as being against Americans. Not an exclusive feature, most people tend to be more defensive of their own under criticism from foreigners, but that is also a particularly strong trend among some very vocal American groups.<br /> <br /> On the other side, anti-American sentiments in <u>some degree</u> are extremely common the world around, so most criticism I've heard from non-Americans about a US president <b><u>was</u></b> also an implicit criticism on Americans as a whole, with at least a hint of being against them.<br /> <br /> This is, again, one of the things Putin and Xi-Jinping capitalize on the whole US position of influence over other powers. From an American and maybe Canadian perspective (I'm not sure in the latter, but seems to be the case), comparing them with the US is ludicrous. From most other people's perspectives... not so much. For a lot of people American interference is a very real and worrying concern. My own country faced 20 years of a military dictatorship with still a lot of unexplained disappearances, unsolved murders and so on to deal with. Our elections still pit against one another victims of war crimes and defenders of the very same crimes as candidates. And the US played a large role in it. This is probably one of the reasons why Ukraine stayed away from NATO for so long.<br /> <br /> Now, the point about Putin's opposition in Russia isn't about not acknowledging him as a head of state, but not acknowledging his <i>legitimacy</i>. Those are two distinct things in international politic. Putin is intimately related to the Russian organized crime and probably a crime boss himself, and his ascension to power was heavily based on criminal activity. This relates to the state of Russia at the end of Gorbachev's tenure, as the fall of the Soviet state actually did included an almost complete collapse of state institutions and government structures.<br /> <br /> Russia was virtually lawless for a long time. You had personnel with access to State assets, including military assets, with no oversight at all of any kind and no possibility of consequences for whatever they decided to do with it. Boris Yeltsin basically oversaw the destruction of the state as the means to transition to capitalism. Beyond this transition being good or bad in itself, the fact is that Yeltsin mismanaged it hugely, caused major economic and political crisis, and basically freed criminals and oligarchs to operate completely unchecked, while corruption soared to the skies.<br /> <br /> So... yes, the call isn't to consider Putin a fake president, but to consider him a criminal that shouldn't be allowed to be president, basically holding his nation hostage more than ruling it. And this is true at least to some extent (and I believe that it is to a huge extent).<br /> <br /> About the PRC, it always has a lot of intrigue because of how Chinese politics work. It is the <i>only</i> party and the <i>de facto</i> ruling body, so <i>every single political intrigue</i> has to happen within the party, with many groups that would be in distinct parties or be their own party in multi-party republics living inside the PRC instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T01:51:33-07:00","id":1476509,"title":"","content":"Russia just began sanctioning US politicians and private citizens. It&quot;'s &quot;interesting&quot; that not a single Republican was targeted with those sanctions. With their Canadian sanctions they hit people from a wide range of political parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T20:18:56-07:00","id":1476757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476420#post1476420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is the opposite. On one hand, a number of Americans get defensive if a foreigner criticize their presidents and take it as being against Americans. Not an exclusive feature, most people tend to be more defensive of their own under criticism from foreigners, but that is also a particularly strong trend among some very vocal American groups.<br /> <br /> On the other side, anti-American sentiments in <u>some degree</u> are extremely common the world around, so most criticism I've heard from non-Americans about a US president <b><u>was</u></b> also an implicit criticism on Americans as a whole, with at least a hint of being against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have had vocal disagreements with people I know IRL about specificity when criticizing the policies and actions of American Government Agencies over which most Americans <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TfQij4aQq1k\" target=\"_blank\">have little influence</a> and many actively object to. It's worth making the effort to name the agency or at least say &quot;the U.S. Government&quot;, rather than &quot;the Americans&quot; did some bad thing. In Canada, it's particularly important if you are out at a restaurant, since we have so many American tourists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476420#post1476420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, again, one of the things Putin and Xi-Jinping capitalize on the whole US position of influence over other powers. From an American and maybe Canadian perspective (I'm not sure in the latter, but seems to be the case), comparing them with the US is ludicrous. From most other people's perspectives... not so much. For a lot of people American interference is a very real and worrying concern. My own country faced 20 years of a military dictatorship with still a lot of unexplained disappearances, unsolved murders and so on to deal with. Our elections still pit against one another victims of war crimes and defenders of the very same crimes as candidates. And the US played a large role in it. This is probably one of the reasons why Ukraine stayed away from NATO for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of unnecessary suffering has been inflicted by the NSA, CIA and the Pentagon on people in Latin America. At a point when I was very close with someone from one such country currently in economic and political crisis, we had this shared sense of powerlessness, only being able to verbally condemn those outsiders who looted the economy of her former homeland and wish for a better future. I still follow events going on there. I was gong to respond to the rest of your reply, but I've gone somewhere.. again.<br /> <br /> Edit: returning to the present..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476420#post1476420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the point about Putin's opposition in Russia isn't about not acknowledging him as a head of state, but not acknowledging his <i>legitimacy</i>. Those are two distinct things in international politic. Putin is intimately related to the Russian organized crime and probably a crime boss himself, and his ascension to power was heavily based on criminal activity. This relates to the state of Russia at the end of Gorbachev's tenure, as the fall of the Soviet state actually did included an almost complete collapse of state institutions and government structures</div> </div> </div> </div>I was glued to the TV back then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476420#post1476420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Russia was virtually lawless for a long time. You had personnel with access to State assets, including military assets, with no oversight at all of any kind and no possibility of consequences for whatever they decided to do with it. Boris Yeltsin basically oversaw the destruction of the state as the means to transition to capitalism. Beyond this transition being good or bad in itself, the fact is that Yeltsin mismanaged it hugely, caused major economic and political crisis, and basically freed criminals and oligarchs to operate completely unchecked, while corruption soared to the skies.<br /> <br /> So... yes, the call isn't to consider Putin a fake president, but to consider him a criminal that shouldn't be allowed to be president, basically holding his nation hostage more than ruling it. And this is true at least to some extent (and I believe that it is to a huge extent).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder about something. Putin addressed families of military conscripts, young men forced to fight in Ukraine. The antiwar movement is quite large. How much of an overlap do you imagine exists between members of the antiwar movement and the families of conscripts? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476420#post1476420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the PRC, it always has a lot of intrigue because of how Chinese politics work. It is the <i>only</i> party and the <i>de facto</i> ruling body, so <i>every single political intrigue</i> has to happen within the party, with many groups that would be in distinct parties or be their own party in multi-party republics living inside the PRC instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a system that oppresses even its rulers. not that I have sympathy to spare for them. I bet they are all spying on each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-20-2022, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T21:00:06-07:00","id":1476758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476509#post1476509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Russia just began sanctioning US politicians and private citizens. It&quot;'s &quot;interesting&quot; that not a single Republican was targeted with those sanctions. With their Canadian sanctions they hit people from a wide range of political parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that it is a feeble attempt to sow discord. As for Canadian politicians, if an MP has a bank account in Russia, I consider that cause for inquiry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T22:30:46-07:00","id":1476761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476757#post1476757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had vocal disagreements with people I know IRL about specificity when criticizing the policies and actions of American Government Agencies over which most Americans <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TfQij4aQq1k\" target=\"_blank\">have little influence</a> and many actively object to. It's worth making the effort to name the agency or at least say &quot;the U.S. Government&quot;, rather than &quot;the Americans&quot; did some bad thing. In Canada, it's particularly important if you are out at a restaurant, since we have so many American tourists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of unnecessary suffering has been inflicted by the NSA, CIA and the Pentagon on people in Latin America. At a point when I was very close with someone from one such country currently in economic and political crisis, we had this shared sense of powerlessness, only being able to verbally condemn those outsiders who looted the economy of her former homeland and wish for a better future. I still follow events going on there. I was gong to respond to the rest of your reply, but I've gone somewhere.. again.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day this is mostly a moot point.<br /> <br /> We can have lengthy discussions on how much responsibility the American people as a whole have on those maters, it doesn't matter. On one hand, most people outside US direct relations won't perceive US people and US government as significantly different. On the other, even for those that do, using the country/group's name to refer to their government/leaders/agencies is just common parlance. Those are the actors of the decisions and negotiations on the matter anyway. Ukraine's government officials are talking with Russia's government officials, they talk about US' government interference and so on. It is pointless to try and specify agencies and institutions every single time when most of the point is which country they're representing, despite we all knowing (at least we should) that things are never that simple in the specific countries.<br /> <br /> Talking about things not being that simple, Russia's sanctions are probably to show off to their own people first, only second to retaliate the sanctions they're getting. It was, seriously, to be expected, and while they may be feeble (I'm not so sure), they're not just a petty move. It is the obvious way to respond to sanctions you receive, regardless of your perceived moral ground. I'm not sure if they are feeble because the world is still globalized and a lot of stuff comes from Russia. Even if no politician in Canada has Russian bank accounts, it doesn't mean they don't have personal commercial interests and partners there, even accounts meant for financial exchange that are perfectly legal and declared. It is actually likely that at least some of them have big investments in Russia or that go through Russia for one reason or another, maybe some commodity exchanges in oil, everything perfectly legal and fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T08:54:31-07:00","id":1476847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476761#post1476761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We can have lengthy discussions on how much responsibility the American people as a whole have on those maters, it doesn't matter. On one hand, most people outside US direct relations won't perceive US people and US government as significantly different. On the other, even for those that do, using the country/group's name to refer to their government/leaders/agencies is just common parlance. Those are the actors of the decisions and negotiations on the matter anyway. Ukraine's government officials are talking with Russia's government officials, they talk about US' government interference and so on. It is pointless to try and specify agencies and institutions every single time when most of the point is which country they're representing, despite we all knowing (at least we should) that things are never that simple in the specific countries.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh don't worry, it's ENTIRELY the people's responsibility here in the USA. These supposed executors of our will do whatever they want to follow their little power plays and forward their own agendas without our knowledge or consent. And it's precisely because a majority of people here in the US are complacent, ignorant, fools who only react to events which directly affect their individual selves. We aren't even adequately taught the basics of civics here in this country, likely to make sure we can't interfere with existing power structures. So yeah, if you ever doubt the responsibility of the American people for the actions our government, remember that all those people retain their positions only because the people are too stupid or too selfish to care.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T12:31:15-07:00","id":1476866,"title":"","content":"Eh... the US system is pretty heavily rigged. While US citizen engagement is a problem, it's hard to get people involved when the system fails them over and over.<br /> <br /> 5 out of the 9 current Supreme Court seats are currently held by Justices appointed by Bush 2 or Trump. Or, in other words, our highest court has a majority appointed by the minority of the voting population. 6 if you count Bryer since Clinton won, but never got 50%+1 of the popular vote (though he's retiring soon). Our Senate gives an inordinate amount of power to population-small farming states (not an accident), and our House is gerrymandered to further ensure the majority vote is diminished in power. The whole reason our highest court has six members that were nominated by Presidents that couldn't get 50%+1 of the popular vote is because of our archaic (and extremely hard to remove) Electoral College system.<br /> <br /> Thanks to decades of propaganda of the US being the &quot;premiere&quot; democracy of the world, a lot of people don't realize how shitty we are at actually being a democracy. They don't understand that it's entirely possible for things to happen directly against the popular vote of the people (that isn't a tyranny of the majority issue) and that the majority of people wanted a different outcome.<br /> <br /> So, yes, more voter engagement would be great. Especially in local elections because the lack of attention to those is the rot at the foundations of all this. But we're not a fair system, and the majority can't just magically vote harder to overcome many of the barriers holding us back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T18:15:32-07:00","id":1476907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476847#post1476847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh don't worry, it's ENTIRELY the people's responsibility here in the USA. These supposed executors of our will do whatever they want to follow their little power plays and forward their own agendas without our knowledge or consent. And it's precisely because a majority of people here in the US are complacent, ignorant, fools who only react to events which directly affect their individual selves. We aren't even adequately taught the basics of civics here in this country, likely to make sure we can't interfere with existing power structures. So yeah, if you ever doubt the responsibility of the American people for the actions our government, remember that all those people retain their positions only because the people are too stupid or too selfish to care.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are Americans who are engaged, aware and who fight for things outside their immediate self interests, like Represent Us and others who keep trying in the face of a well organized corporate political class. A person who does everything to fight <i>against</i> what a government agency is doing or to reverse the damage it has done should not be lumped in with it as &quot;the Americans did it&quot;. It's the presumption of innocence and the value of seeking out the best examples of a population, not the worst or the pacified. The fact that someone has been pacified means a crime was committed against them, beginning when they were a psychologically defenseless infant viewing advertising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T07:56:06-07:00","id":1476960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1476907#post1476907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are Americans who are engaged, aware and who fight for things outside their immediate self interests, like Represent Us and others who keep trying in the face of a well organized corporate political class. A person who does everything to fight <i>against</i> what a government agency is doing or to reverse the damage it has done should not be lumped in with it as &quot;the Americans did it&quot;. It's the presumption of innocence and the value of seeking out the best examples of a population, not the worst or the pacified. The fact that someone has been pacified means a crime was committed against them, beginning when they were a psychologically defenseless infant viewing advertising.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're reading too much into this.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know the issues both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar765_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"765\" data-vbnamecard=\"765\">Darksol-aeternium</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> cited and they're both real. And we can dig into this tangent to discuss a lot of relevant stuff. The US does currently have one of the weakest democratic systems, maybe because it virtually got no upgrade in the past two centuries while everyone else modernized, it just poorly patched some leaks. And the people does have some responsibility over it as they do indeed mostly accept the system.<br /> <br /> But one way or the other this is the kind of discussion where generalizations are just a means to make the discussion possible. Some people will take the generalization at face value, but those people won't listen to you if you try to explain nuance anyway. When we say &quot;Americans&quot; no one here is saying that this applies to all Americans, or even to most Americans. It is just that for <i>those discussions</i> going in detail as to how many Americans think like that, or how exactly each social component of the country contributes to it or against it would just derail the conversation.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Americans do that in wars&quot; doesn't mean every American would do that, every American agree with that, every American is aware or anything like that. It simply means &quot;The Americans&quot; in the context of the conversation. When Darksol says &quot;the American people is responsible&quot; it doesn't means every American is personally responsible, it means &quot;in general terms there's a greater number of people in the country with attitudes that in one way or another contributes to the problem, regardless of intention or awareness and not necessarily the same attitudes among them, than people with attitudes that in one way or another contribute to its correction, and there are reasons why this shouldn't be the case, hence we can conclude that most of those people has some measure of responsibility even if not the same measure or for the same reasons among them&quot;. But that's a useless mouthful, imagine having to repeat such things <i>ad nauseam </i>for every nation cited in a conversation about international affairs?<br /> <br /> All this applies equally to every country. Some people get it and know generalizations are just tools for easing speech, some people don't, but they're almost certainly too bigoted to care anyway, and when the confusion arrives it is usually more productive to talk with people reading it at face value as an aside than really introducing repetitive disclaimers all over the conversation.<br /> <br /> We're all aware that government decisions and actions face a greater range of debate, polemic and resistance in their own countries, and this is true for the US, Russia, France, UK, Brazil, Belarus, China... reading about their internal politics is actually pretty interesting and relevant on itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T10:10:56-07:00","id":1476977,"title":"","content":"Because I sometimes follow what's going on in the chess world, I thought I would share some news I came across. <span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Sergey Karjakin, a</span> Russian player in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIDE\" target=\"_blank\">FIDE</a> tournaments was banned by FIDE for statements he made on Twitter in support of Putin and the invasion of Ukraine. In the first four minutes of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dieM4IDbJsQ\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a>, Levi Rozman discusses this news, as well as Daniil Medvedev, a Russian Tennis player facing pressure to denounce Putin, commenting that it is not fair to expect someone living under a dangerously repressive regime to speak out against it.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-22-2022, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T17:22:22-07:00","id":1477039,"title":"","content":"By not choosing a side, I think Daniil Medvedev will make it worse for themself. While their point is valid, the world (and people as a consequence) isn\u2019t fair. I expect they will soon be forced pick a side and suffer the consequences for both doing so and for stalling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T16:37:05-07:00","id":1477131,"title":"","content":"I agree that it isn't fair to expect someone to speak against their own regime when there's something at stake for them, and that isn't just on dangerously repressive regimes. Weren't Putin perfectly inclined to send killers against them even in other countries, Russian athletes would still be particularly dependent on federal support AFAIK, so siding against it may be career suicide. It is another matter entirely from choosing to actively support the regime.<br /> <br /> But that aside, we're talking about several people making valid decisions. Who am I to berate an organization, team, athlete or fan that thinks what they can do to help against a crisis is to demand your support before throwing theirs to you? It is complicated.<br /> <br /> On this case, though, I think not picking a side is already a good compromise that should be respected. Precisely because the Russian regime is that oppressive you can bet there's also a lot of pressure for them to support Putin. Just by not doing that they're already walking a dangerous line. I wouldn't ask for more without being at the very least able to literally rescue them from danger and offer some solid protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T17:03:01-07:00","id":1477135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1475571-russia-s-war-on-ukraine?p=1477131#post1477131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it isn't fair to expect someone to speak against their own regime when there's something at stake for them, and that isn't just on dangerously repressive regimes. Weren't Putin perfectly inclined to send killers against them even in other countries, Russian athletes would still be particularly dependent on federal support AFAIK, so siding against it may be career suicide. It is another matter entirely from choosing to actively support the regime.<br /> <br /> But that aside, we're talking about several people making valid decisions. Who am I to berate an organization, team, athlete or fan that thinks what they can do to help against a crisis is to demand your support before throwing theirs to you? It is complicated.<br /> <br /> On this case, though, I think not picking a side is already a good compromise that should be respected. Precisely because the Russian regime is that oppressive you can bet there's also a lot of pressure for them to support Putin. Just by not doing that they're already walking a dangerous line. I wouldn't ask for more without being at the very least able to literally rescue them from danger and offer some solid protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've saved me the effort of what I was formulating. Exactly what I would say about that. The most recent thing I heard was about Russians being coerced into participating in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fCmOJYaN1t4\" target=\"_blank\">pro-Putin rallies</a> (Zed Rallies?), where they have to form into a Zed and have pre-scripted answers to give reporters about their reasons for being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}